  "limitations": [
    "Candidate source is a sanitized export of SpaceApp stable eebf761963 (4362 files), the 1.1.6 release-train cutoff; the public candidate a43e799 adds the launcher install telemetry and the launcher review fixes F4, F7 and F8 on top of 1.1.5.",
    "VM hosts are x86_64. ARM64 container validation remains a release workflow gate.",
    "Fresh installer timings use preloaded local candidate images; they exclude network image downloads.",
    "The 1.1.5 -> 1.1.6 update ran on each retained original installation, which the 1.1.5 release lab left at 1.1.5.",
    "Windows desktop commands ran as interactive scheduled tasks in an owned RDP session; this is not keystroke coverage of every wizard prompt.",
    "Install telemetry Yes ran on Linux only, on a separate owned fixture purged afterwards: the spaceapp.dev collector log holds exactly one install_started, install_completed, setup_completed, first_cli (opencode), first_answer and active event with the fixture's install id, all marked internal (lab address; the IP is not stored), and the first_answer marker did not change after a second finished answer. Telemetry No on all three systems: no install id, no marker, and no lab event at the collector from the install through the agent sequence.",
    "Small-profile memory (known since 1.1.5, unchanged in 1.1.6): on Linux the CLI container (2 GiB limit) recorded one out-of-memory kill during the full first-session flow, so the two-native-panes check failed in the sequence; rerun alone after a VM restart it passed with no kill. Several simultaneous OpenCode panes need the medium profile.",
    "Profiles ran one VM boot per sequence under the 20 GiB host memory floor; every runner was reverted to 8 GiB/4 CPU. Three attempts stopped before the product ran because the lab desktop was not ready within 15 minutes after the memory change (Windows RDP session dropped twice, macOS Docker Desktop once); each passed on the next attempt.",
    "Automatic browser opening was evidenced on Linux (lab Chrome CDP page list right after the install) and macOS (console capture); Windows ran the install with open=yes in the signed-in desktop, but no desktop capture was taken.",
    "Update badge: a 1.1.6 candidate is never older than the GitHub latest release, so on the owned fixture only spaceapp-core was recreated reporting SPACE_APP_VERSION=1.1.4 (same image and data) against the real GitHub latest 1.1.5; it was then restored and the real 1.1.6 showed no badge.",
    "The public suite's SQLite worker tests need Python 3.12 or newer (sqlite-worker.py uses an f-string with a backslash); they pass on GitHub's ubuntu-latest runners and fail in a Debian bookworm container (Python 3.11). The spaceapp-core image has no python3, so the SQLite Databases worker cannot run in public installations (1.1.7).",
    "Review findings deferred to 1.1.7: digest-pinned first-party images (#9), provenance of public-only files (F9), F14 (Cursor download checksum, npm lockfiles and install scripts, Docker apt key fingerprint, Authenticode subject) and F16 (.trivyignore wording).",
    "npm next publication, environment approval and latest promotion have not yet completed."
  ]
